WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:04.520
- We are announcing our plan
to stay ahead of this virus

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.630
by being prepared to offer
COVID-19 booster shots

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:12.750
to fully vaccinated
adults 18 years and older.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.410
They would be eligible
for their booster shot

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.330
eight months after
receiving their second dose

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.680
of the Pfizer or Moderna mRNA vaccines.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.680
We plan to start this program

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:27.680
the week of September 20th, 2021.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:29.840
- [Narrator] The Biden
administration booster announcement

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.990
comes amid reports of fully
vaccinated people getting COVID,

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:36.200
cases known as breakthrough infections.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.250
This includes a Wall
Street Journal analysis

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.270
that found the Delta
variant is breaking through

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:43.550
vaccine protection at a higher
rate than other strains.

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:45.180
- I wanna be very clear.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.800
This plan is pending the FDA conducting

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:52.391
an independent evaluation of
the safety and effectiveness

00:00:52.391 --> 00:00:56.610
of a third dose of the Pfizer
and Moderna mRNA vaccines

00:00:56.610 --> 00:01:01.490
and the CDC's advisory committee
on immunization practices

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.750
issuing booster dose recommendations

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.950
based on a thorough
review of the evidence.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.840
- [Narrator] Here's why
a third-dose booster shot

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.970
of mRNA vaccines is now recommended

00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:12.258
for fully vaccinated people.

00:01:12.258 --> 00:01:13.290
(bell dinging)

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.430
Data suggests that while
vaccines are still shown

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:16.850
to be highly effective,

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.100
as antibodies begin to dwindle naturally,

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.110
the protection vaccines
offer it can wane over time.

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:24.470
The mRNA boosters that
the Biden administration

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:26.860
is recommending could have a big impact.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:28.800
Studies show that they
generate higher levels

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.890
of neutralizing antibodies
than just two doses alone.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:35.080
Neutralizing antibodies are
the ones primarily responsible

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.350
for stopping the virus
from entering cells.

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:40.340
- Antibodies are seen as providing

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:44.580
some of that initial
protection against the virus,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:47.180
potentially stopping
infection from happening

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.910
and from the virus from spreading.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:53.310
The reason why we are seeing
vaccines still hold up

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:56.370
and be effective at
preventing hospitalization

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:58.800
or severe disease or death

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.210
is because of other parts
of the immune system,

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:02.820
what's known as the
adaptive immune system,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.300
such as T cells or memory B cells.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:08.077
T cells actually identify, seek out,

00:02:08.077 --> 00:02:10.610
and destroy the infected cells.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:13.020
- [Narrator] The mRNA vaccine
makers have released data

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:15.270
showing that antibody
levels have increased

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:16.650
following booster shots,

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.780
and Pfizer and partner
BioNTech are planning

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.800
to seek clearance from the
FDA for a COVID-19 booster

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.130
for the general population.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.210
The company said they sent the FDA results

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:26.890
from a small early stage studies

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:30.100
showing a third dose of
vaccines generated higher levels

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.200
of neutralizing antibodies
against the original virus,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.450
as well as the Beta and Delta variants.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.890
The third dose appeared
safe in the trial as well.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.530
The Biden administration is
recommending that booster shots

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:42.820
for the general public be
taken about eight months

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.390
after the second dose of mRNA vaccines.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.070
But for some who are immunocompromised

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:48.790
and don't have a strong immune response

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.000
to the standard two-course
vaccine regimen,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.280
booster shots could be needed even sooner.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.170
The current guidance in
the CDC is that those

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.790
who are moderately to
severely immunocompromised

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.270
should take a third
dose of an mRNA vaccine

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:02.930
at least 28 days after the second shot.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.330
- Immunocompromised people
is a very broad term

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.690
that includes people who
are transplant patients,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.800
so if you have a kidney transplant.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.690
It can include some cancer patients.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.630
Basically individuals whose immune systems

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.510
don't necessarily respond
like the general populations.

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:24.780
- [Narrator] Some of those
who fall into this category

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.120
should be able to walk
into certain clinics

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.890
to get a booster shot now,

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.470
but for the general population,

00:03:30.470 --> 00:03:33.070
boosters have not yet
been approved by the FDA,

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:35.220
which gives final approval on vaccines.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.510
Pfizer is the furthest along

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.460
in the regulatory approval process,

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:42.000
but Moderna, which also produces
a two-dose mRNA vaccine,

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.130
said it plans to ask regulators next month

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.420
to authorize booster shots as well.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.840
- The plan ensures that people
who were fully vaccinated

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:50.880
earliest in the vaccination rollout

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:53.580
will be eligible for a booster first.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.280
This includes our most
vulnerable populations,

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.280
like our healthcare providers,
nursing home residents,

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.440
and other seniors.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.020
- [Narrator] Johnson &amp;
Johnson does not make

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.420
an mRNA vaccine,

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.090
which means the current
booster guidelines won't apply.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:09.410
- For people who received the
Johnson &amp; Johnson vaccine,

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:13.610
we anticipate vaccine boosters
will likely be needed.

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:16.980
The J &amp; J vaccine was not
administered in the U.S.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.407
until March of 2021,

00:04:19.407 --> 00:04:23.010
and we expect more data on
J &amp; J in the coming weeks.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.920
- [Narrator] The company's
expected to release data

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:28.400
about the efficacy of two doses
of its single-shot vaccine

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.390
later this month.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.020
The White House has
said that it is prepared

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.810
with enough extra vaccine orders

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:34.750
if the FDA approves the booster.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.950
- That is why we ordered the
number of doses we did order

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:40.760
several months ago because
we are like boy scouts

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.855
and girl scouts and
always wanna be prepared.

00:04:42.855 --> 00:04:45.438
(bell dinging)

